	<h2>14. Reconstruction</h2>
	<div class="content-content">




<figure class="wp-block-image alignwide size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="587" src="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/contraband1-1024x587.jpg" alt="“Contrabands,” Cumberland Landing, Virginia, 1862. Library of Congress. Photograph of over a dozen African Americans sitting or standing in front of a cabin. They range in age from children to the elderly. " class="wp-image-1334" srcset="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/contraband1-1024x587.jpg 1024w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/contraband1-300x172.jpg 300w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/contraband1-768x441.jpg 768w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/contraband1.jpg 1400w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Figure 14.1. “Contrabands,” Cumberland Landing, Virginia, 1862. Library of Congress.</figcaption></figure>







